Subject: src/xz/file_io.c: on OpenVMS, st_ino is an array only without _USE_STD_STAT

xz's VMS code clears st_ino as the array of three words that the
traditional VMS struct stat has.  With _USE_STD_STAT (which the OpenVMS
ports build with, for 64-bit inode numbers and the standard layout) st_ino
is one 64-bit number, and the code did not compile (%CC-E-NEEDPOINTER).
Use the array form only without _USE_STD_STAT; the comparison elsewhere
uses memcmp and works with either.

--- a/src/xz/file_io.c	2026-10-05 11:03:46.566080307 +0100
+++ b/src/xz/file_io.c	2026-10-05 11:03:46.590480513 +0100
@@ -986,7 +986,7 @@
 
 	if (fstat(pair->dest_fd, &pair->dest_st)) {
 		// If fstat() really fails, we have a safe fallback here.
-#if defined(__VMS)
+#if defined(__VMS) && !defined(_USE_STD_STAT)
 		pair->dest_st.st_ino[0] = 0;
 		pair->dest_st.st_ino[1] = 0;
 		pair->dest_st.st_ino[2] = 0;
